When observing a galaxy completely analogous to the Milky Way, an outburst of a nova was detected at a distance of 6 kpc from its centre. The apparent magnitude of the galaxy is $10^\mathrm{m}$, and the galaxy itself is observed as an ellipse with a ratio of semi-axes of $5:3$. Determine:
a. the distance to the galaxy;
b. the possible values of the observed radial velocity of the nova;
c. the possible angular distances between the centre of the galaxy and the nova.
Neglect interstellar and intergalactic absorption, and also the influence of other galaxies on the observed quantities.
